The executions for proposals aedfc67459cd985d and f959cb65a7a01b40 both show that the kernel `conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose` moved from 'no' to 'yes' when the transform `conformance.transform.prose-after` was applied to a strict JSON object. This confirms the expectation that adding prose after the JSON object forces the harness to use its recovery logic rather than reading the reply as strict JSON, as defined in the registry [eb9c082f3ea034d3]. Similarly, proposal 6d40d26faae48dbc showed that `conformance.kernel.recovery` moved when `conformance.transform.upper-case` was applied, as the recovered object's keys and values were capitalized, changing the canonical JSON representation [c5afea8a28ed0472].